  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "Why isn't my porcelain tile lasting?",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "HH Remodeling LLC"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
    "url": "http://coloradoremodeling.company"
  },
  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you invest in a new porcelain tile floor and it doesn't hold up like you expected, right? Often, the culprit isn't the tile itself, but what happened *during* installation. One big reason for early failure is poor surface preparation. If the subfloor isn't clean, smooth, dry, and perfectly level, you're setting yourself up for trouble. We've seen cracking and lippage—that unevenness between tiles—happen a lot because of this. Another common issue is using the wrong adhesive or not letting it cure properly. Standard-set adhesive needs about 24 hours before you even walk on it, and grout often needs a good 72 hours before heavy use. Rushing these steps can really compromise the whole installation's integrity. Also, sometimes people forget about expansion joints, especially for large areas or outdoor installations. These joints are crucial for allowing the tile to expand and contract with temperature changes, preventing cracks. If you're seeing problems, it might be worth having a pro take a look to diagnose what went wrong. Don't worry, sometimes it's fixable, and sometimes you just learn for the next project! If you're dealing with failing tile, give HH Remodeling LLC a call.",
